# Applications and the package-management front ends.

# --- Software center ------------------------------------------------------
# gnome-software is the one front end that handles deb, snap and flatpak
# together. Ubuntu's own App Center is a Flutter snap and cannot list debs.
gnome-software
gnome-software-plugin-snap
gnome-software-plugin-flatpak

# --- the three packaging systems -----------------------------------------
snapd
flatpak

# --- printing and scanning (R-04: an on-disc group) -----------------------
# Named drivers, not printer-driver-all, which is hundreds of megabytes of
# vendor blobs for printers nobody here owns. gutenprint and escpr between
# them cover most of what people actually plug in; everything modern is
# driverless over IPP anyway, which is what sane-airscan and ipp-usb are for.
cups
cups-client
cups-filters
system-config-printer
avahi-daemon
simple-scan
printer-driver-gutenprint
printer-driver-escpr
sane-airscan
ipp-usb

# --- media (R-04: an on-disc group) ---------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT ubuntu-restricted-extras. That pulls
# ttf-mscorefonts-installer, which downloads fonts from the network while it
# configures -- so an offline install would fail on the one group that exists
# to work offline. The codecs are named directly and the fonts left out.
gstreamer1.0-plugins-good
gstreamer1.0-plugins-bad
gstreamer1.0-plugins-ugly
gstreamer1.0-libav
libavcodec-extra
vlc

# --- Thai ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Without these, Thai renders as boxes and cannot be typed at all.
fonts-thai-tlwg
fonts-noto-cjk
language-pack-th
language-pack-gnome-th
ibus
ibus-libthai
libthai-data

# --- installer -------------------------------------------------------------
calamares
calamares-settings-ubuntu-common

# --- misc ------------------------------------------------------------------
xdg-desktop-portal
xdg-desktop-portal-gtk
xdg-user-dirs
xdg-utils
gparted
